    rdf:value """Monday, Nov. 4, 1907
Clearing up.
Rothenstein.
Bernhard and Rothenstein went to Santa Maria Novella and were joined by Gordon Craig. Rothenstein stayed down to lunch.
I called for Maud Cruttwell at 3.30, and we went up to the Villa Curonia, the Dodges’. They’ve spent a million on making it hideous. She is an oriental sort of creature — though American — lazy and luxury loving, and fortunately rich. She seems an ordinary sort of person."""^^xsd:string ;
    mbdiaries-ontology:index 330 ;
    mbdiaries-ontology:part_of <https://mbdiaries.itatti.harvard.edu/resource/diary/1907> .

